  "subject": "science",
  "summary": "A semester of high school biology built around investigation: cells and transport, heredity, cell energy, DNA and proteins, evolution by natural selection, and ecology. Six units, each with a student overview, a teacher guide with a five-day plan, a hands-on lab or simulation, assignments that analyze real-world data and argue from evidence, an assessment with a rubric and an answer key. Science has no built-in standards framework, so activities align honestly to the CCSS literacy standards for science and technical subjects and, where students analyze data, to high school statistics.",
  "title": "Biology I",
